WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.776
AI made self-hosting

00:00:01.588 --> 00:00:02.425
fun again

00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:03.641
A look at

00:00:03.453 --> 00:00:04.726
how AI assistance

00:00:04.538 --> 00:00:05.835
has made self-hosting

00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:06.542
fun again

00:00:06.682 --> 00:00:07.695
I never really

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.745
stopped self-hosting

00:00:08.804 --> 00:00:09.735
but I became

00:00:09.547 --> 00:00:10.466
less inclined to

00:00:10.278 --> 00:00:11.457
experiment with new

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:11.999
things

00:00:12.526 --> 00:00:13.516
There were times

00:00:13.328 --> 00:00:13.905
when I was

00:00:13.717 --> 00:00:14.967
quite enthusiastic

00:00:14.778 --> 00:00:15.367
about it

00:00:15.462 --> 00:00:16.570
constantly trying out

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:17.750
new software and

00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:18.445
tinkering with my

00:00:18.257 --> 00:00:19.235
infrastructure

00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:20.626
Over the last

00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:21.782
few months however

00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:22.832
I’ve found myself

00:00:22.643 --> 00:00:23.787
getting increasingly

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:25.190
excited about self-hosting

00:00:25.002 --> 00:00:25.638
again

00:00:25.777 --> 00:00:26.850
Maintaining what I

00:00:26.674 --> 00:00:27.652
already had running

00:00:27.464 --> 00:00:28.135
was enough for

00:00:27.947 --> 00:00:28.395
me

00:00:28.926 --> 00:00:29.940
Full story on

00:00:29.751 --> 00:00:30.647
the dashboard
